  "stem": "The function \\(f\\) is defined by \\(f(x) = a(x - 3)^{2} + 2\\), where \\(a\\) is a constant. The graph of \\(y = f(x)\\) in the \\(xy\\)-plane crosses the \\(y\\)-axis at \\((0, 20)\\). What is the value of \\(f(5)\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "10"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Use the \\(y\\)-intercept: \\(f(0) = a(0 - 3)^{2} + 2 = 9a + 2 = 20\\), so \\(a = 2\\).",
    "Then \\(f(x) = 2(x - 3)^{2} + 2\\).",
    "\\(f(5) = 2(2)^{2} + 2 = 10\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "a, x = symbols('a x')\nf = a*(x - 3)**2 + 2\nav = solve(Eq(f.subs(x, 0), 20), a)\nassert av == [2]\nassert f.subs({a: 2, x: 5}) == 10 == Rational(spr_answers[0])",
